This is a simple recursion problem.

We can go from top to bottom (i.e., 2 ^ n -->  1) and build the tree based on the return value of the four children.

(1) if the number of element in the grid region is 1, this is a leaf node, we build a new node and return it;
(2) check the four children, if they all are leaf nodes and have the same value, we can merge the four nodes by create a new leaf node;
(3) otherwise, just build a new node from the four children.


